---
/**
 * Targets "hvac seo" (480 searches a month in the US, 40 in Florida, DataForSEO Google Ads, 2026-11-23).
 * Every number on this page is one real client's, with its dates:
 *  - Search numbers: Google Search Console, pulled 2026-11-23 (see Results.astro).
 *  - Profile numbers: Google Business Profile performance, read 2026-11-22.
 *  - Map check: 25-point grid for the client's main repair search, 2026-11-17.
 * The client is not named here (client names only on the Results page).
 */
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/sections/PageHero.astro';
import Results from '@/components/sections/Results.astro';
import FAQ from '@/components/sections/FAQ.astro';
import FinalCTA from '@/components/sections/FinalCTA.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/ui/Icon.astro';
import { SITE, CTA, telHref } from '@/config/site';

const path = '/hvac-seo/';
const h1 = 'HVAC SEO in Palm Beach County';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'Is SEO worth it for an HVAC company?', a: 'For the HVAC contractor on this page, clicks from Google search went from 14 to 43 in 28 days, and calls from the Google Business Profile went from 4 in June 2026 to 9 in October 2026. Whether that pays for you depends on what a job is worth to you and how many of those calls you book. We look at that on the free audit.' },
  { q: 'How long does HVAC SEO take?', a: 'For this client the new website went live on September 21, 2026, and the numbers on this page compare August with late October and November. That is about two months after launch. It is one client, so treat it as an example and not a promise.' },
  { q: 'How much does HVAC SEO cost?', a: 'It depends on what your company needs and where your website and Google Business Profile start today. We go over pricing on the free audit call.' },
  { q: 'Do you work with HVAC companies outside Palm Beach County?', a: 'Our office is in Royal Palm Beach and our clients are local businesses in Palm Beach County. The audit is by phone or video, so ask us if you are nearby.' },
];
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: h1, url: path }];
const pageLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: h1,
  serviceType: 'HVAC SEO',
  url: `${SITE.url}${path}`,
  provider: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#business` },
  areaServed: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'Palm Beach County, FL' },
};
const profile = [
  { label: 'Calls from the Google Business Profile in a month', from: '4', to: '9' },
  { label: 'Requests for directions in a month', from: '0', to: '75' },
  { label: 'All actions on the profile in a month', from: '18', to: '101' },
];
---
<Base
  title="HVAC SEO in Palm Beach County | West Palm Beach SEO"
  description="HVAC SEO for air conditioning companies in Palm Beach County. See one client's Google numbers before and after, with the dates. Book a free audit."
  faqs={faqs}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  schema={[pageLd]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow={SITE.name} title={h1}>
    <p class="lede fade-in mt-7" style="--d:320ms">HVAC SEO is the work that puts an air conditioning company in front of people on Google and Google Maps when their AC stops working.</p>
    <p class="lede fade-in mt-3" style="--d:320ms">West Palm Beach SEO does that work for HVAC companies in Palm Beach County. Below is what it did for one of them, with the dates on every number.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-4 sm:gap-6 fade-in" style="--d:420ms">
      <a href={CTA.primary.href} class="btn btn-primary btn-lg btn-shine">{CTA.primary.label}<Icon name="arrow-right" size={18} /></a>
      <a href={telHref} class="text-[17px] font-semibold text-white inline-flex items-center gap-2"><Icon name="phone" size={17} class="text-gold-300" />{SITE.phone}</a>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <Results only="hvac" title="One HVAC contractor, before and after" surface="surface-cream" />

  <section class="surface-sand py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="container-x max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="h3 text-ink-900">What changed on its Google Business Profile</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">The first number is June 2026. The second is October 2026.</p>
      <dl class="mt-4 divide-y divide-ink-900/10 border-y border-ink-900/10">
        {profile.map((s) => (
          <div class="py-3 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
            <dt class="text-[16px] leading-snug text-ink-600">{s.label}</dt>
            <dd class="shrink-0 text-[19px] font-semibold text-ink-900 whitespace-nowrap"><span class="text-ink-600 font-medium">{s.from}</span><span class="mx-2 text-gold-500" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span><span class="sr-only"> to </span>{s.to}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600/90">Source: the profile's own performance report in Google, read on November 22, 2026. Most of the gain is people asking for directions. Calls went from 4 to 9, which is a small number either way.</p>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="h3 text-ink-900">What we did for this HVAC company</h2>
        <ul class="hvac-list mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          <li>Rebuilt the website so each service has its own page: AC repair, AC installation, and maintenance. The new site went live on September 21, 2026.</li>
          <li>Added a page for each town it serves, 16 in all, each written about that town.</li>
          <li>Cleaned up the Google Business Profile: the service list and the main phone number.</li>
          <li>Asked Google to index the new pages.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="h3 text-ink-900">What is not done yet</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">On November 17, 2026 we checked Google's map results for the company's main repair search from 25 points across its home town. It was in the top three at 18 of the 25. It shows up on the east side of town and drops out to the west and north.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">Clicks also did not climb in a straight line. The 28 days from September 25 to October 22 had 60 clicks, more than the 43 in the latest period. Fewer people searched for the company by name in the latest period, while clicks from searches like "ac repair" plus a town went up.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">We show this because a page with only good numbers should make you ask what was left out.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="h3 text-ink-900">What we check first on an HVAC company's Google profile</h2>
        <ul class="hvac-list mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          <li>The primary category matches the work you want most, such as Air conditioning repair service or HVAC contractor.</li>
          <li>The service list names every job you take: repair, installation, maintenance, duct work.</li>
          <li>The phone number and business name match your website exactly.</li>
          <li>The photos are your own trucks and your own installs.</li>
          <li>Reviews keep coming in, and each one gets a reply.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">You can run the same check yourself with our <a class="text-navy-700 font-semibold underline" href="/google-business-profile-checklist/">free Google Business Profile checklist</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="h3 text-ink-900">Pages an HVAC website needs</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">Google ranks pages, not whole websites. An HVAC company with one services page only shows up for the searches that one page matches.</p>
        <ul class="hvac-list mt-4 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink-600">
          <li>One page per service.</li>
          <li>One page per town you want work in, with real detail about that town.</li>
          <li>A contact page with the same name, address, and phone number as your Google profile.</li>
          <li>Answers to the questions people ask before they call.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12">
        <h2 class="h3 text-ink-900">Related pages</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 text-[17px]">
          <li><a class="text-navy-700 font-semibold underline" href="/">West Palm Beach SEO</a></li>
          <li><a class="text-navy-700 font-semibold underline" href="/services/">SEO services</a></li>
          <li><a class="text-navy-700 font-semibold underline" href="/web-design-west-palm-beach/">Web design in West Palm Beach</a></li>
          <li><a class="text-navy-700 font-semibold underline" href="/seo-boca-raton/">SEO in Boca Raton</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FAQ faqs={faqs} title="Questions about HVAC SEO" surface="surface-cream" />
  <FinalCTA />
</Base>

<style>
  .hvac-list { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.2em; display: grid; gap: .5em; }
  .hvac-list li::marker { color: var(--color-gold-500); }
</style>
